From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:05:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: sn201202x: Wake from suspend-to-idle for a
 new USB link

A USB device plugged into a J713 in suspend-to-idle cannot wake it, and
cannot wake it later either: an idle USB-C port is powered down, so the
device is never enumerated. Only the Type-C controller notices it: its
event interrupt fires for the attach even while it sleeps.

As a plain wakeup source that interrupt would also wake the system for
a charger, on every plug, unplug and power negotiation. Filter the
events instead. With wakeup-source set, the event interrupt stays live
in system sleep (IRQF_NO_SUSPEND) and sn201202x_sleep_event() handles
it there: it wakes the controller, acknowledges its events, reads its
data status and status, and wakes the system with pm_wakeup_dev_event()
only for a link that was not there before:

 - a USB2 or USB3 link with the port as the host: a port attaches as a
   USB device, as to a charger, before any data role swap;
 - from a power source, only one capable of USB communication, as its
   first source capability PDO says: a charger may still report a USB
   link as host for a moment after the swap;
 - DisplayPort, Thunderbolt or USB4.

A charger plugged in or unplugged leaves the system asleep. A read that
fails wakes it. The controller goes back to sleep either way, and the
resume revalidates the whole port as before. A controller reset seen in
sleep is set up again on resume, as cd321x_check_setup() latches it.

The interrupt is not armed for wakeup, so IRQF_NO_SUSPEND is used as
Documentation/power/suspend-and-interrupts.rst describes for a handler
that decides itself whether to wake the system, with pm_system_wakeup()
underneath. The watch is set up for suspend-to-idle only.

In suspend-to-idle the tick is frozen, so a sleeping wait does not end
until something else wakes the system: the controller is polled with
busy waits there, within a fixed budget, and WAKEUP is repeated in case
it reached a controller still going to sleep. A resume whose WAKEUP is
not confirmed now falls back to polling as well. Its other interrupts
are suspended, so this needs a controller without select notification,
as on T8132; others keep their behaviour. A transfer the SPMI controller
never answers still waits on its timer, so it ends only once the system
is awake again. The port's power/wakeup setting turns the wakeup off.

KUnit cases cover the link decision with the data status and status as
read on a J713 for a charger as it attaches, swaps and settles, and for
a USB keyboard.

The tipd_init() host test stubs gain sleep_event and IRQF_NO_SUSPEND,
and the SN201202x transport test covers the atomic selection too.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>

(cherry picked from commit f738b993b715e1d964f88474244fee2569769206)
[j604 backport: non-built files kept as in our tree: tools/testing/selftests/drivers/apple/sn201202x-transport.py tools/testing/selftests/drivers/gpu/apple-dcp/transaction.py]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig             |   3 +-
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c              |  71 ++++++++++-
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/sn201202x-pm-test.c |  43 +++++++
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c              | 141 +++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h          |  17 +++
 5 files changed, 257 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig
index 6cc0e1d860..83cd877951 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig
@@ -75,5 +75,6 @@ config TYPEC_SN201202X_KUNIT_TEST
 	help
 	  Test that the SN201202x events are not handled while the controller
 	  sleeps, and that a system suspend that fails leaves the controller
-	  awake. These tests run on a simulated SPMI bus, without accessing a
+	  awake. Also test which data status and status count as a link
+	  that wakes the system from suspend-to-idle. These tests run on a simulated SPMI bus, without accessing a
 	  physical Type-C controller.
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
index 33863b9203..09046ebc61 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/power_supply.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
+#include <linux/unaligned.h>
+#include <linux/usb/pd.h>
 #include <linux/usb/typec.h>
 #include <linux/usb/typec_altmode.h>
 #include <linux/usb/typec_dp.h>
@@ -46,6 +48,7 @@
 #define TPS_REG_SYSTEM_CONF		0x28
 #define TPS_REG_CTRL_CONF		0x29
 #define TPS_REG_BOOT_STATUS		0x2D
+#define TPS_REG_RX_SOURCE_CAPS		0x30
 #define TPS_REG_POWER_STATUS		0x3f
 #define TPS_REG_PD_STATUS		0x40
 #define TPS_REG_RX_IDENTITY_SOP		0x48
@@ -1564,6 +1567,46 @@ static int cd321x_check_setup(struct cd321x *cd321x, u64 event)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/**
+ * cd321x_sleep_events - Acknowledge the events of a controller in system sleep
+ * @tps: The controller, woken for this
+ * @st: Its data status and status, and for a power sink whether its source is
+ *	capable of USB communication
+ *
+ * The resume revalidates the whole port state, so nothing else is read.
+ *
+ * Context: tps->lock held.
+ * Return: 0, or a negative error code.
+ */
+int cd321x_sleep_events(struct tps6598x *tps, struct cd321x_sleep_state *st)
+{
+	/* The PDO count, then the first PDO, vSafe5V, which carries the flags */
+	u8 caps[1 + sizeof(u32)];
+	u64 event;
+	int ret;
+
+	lockdep_assert_held(&tps->lock);
+	st->usb_comm = false;
+	ret = tps6598x_read64(tps, TPS_REG_INT_EVENT1, &event);
+	if (!ret && event)
+		ret = tps6598x_write64(tps, TPS_REG_INT_CLEAR1, event);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	/* A controller that was reset is set up again on resume */
+	cd321x_check_setup(container_of(tps, struct cd321x, tps), event);
+
+	ret = tps6598x_read32(tps, TPS_REG_DATA_STATUS, &st->data_status);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = tps6598x_read32(tps, TPS_REG_STATUS, &st->status);
+	if (!ret && !(st->status & TPS_STATUS_PORTROLE)) {
+		ret = tps6598x_block_read(tps, TPS_REG_RX_SOURCE_CAPS, caps, sizeof(caps));
+		if (!ret && (caps[0] & GENMASK(2, 0)))
+			st->usb_comm = get_unaligned_le32(&caps[1]) & PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM;
+	}
+	return ret;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(cd321x_sleep_events);
+
 static irqreturn_t cd321x_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	struct tps6598x *tps = data;
@@ -1572,6 +1615,9 @@ static irqreturn_t cd321x_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	u32 status;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (tps->sleep_event && tps->sleep_event(tps))
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+
 	mutex_lock(&tps->lock);
 
 	ret = tps6598x_read64(tps, TPS_REG_INT_EVENT1, &event);
@@ -2754,10 +2800,17 @@ int tipd_init(struct tps6598x *tps)
 		}
 	}
 
+	tps->wakeup = device_property_read_bool(tps->dev, "wakeup-source");
 	if (tps->irq) {
+		/*
+		 * A variant that filters its events in system sleep keeps the
+		 * interrupt live and decides itself whether to wake the system.
+		 */
 		ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(tps->dev, tps->irq, NULL,
 						tps->data->irq_handler,
-						IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_ONESHOT,
+						IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_ONESHOT |
+						(tps->wakeup && tps->sleep_event ?
+						 IRQF_NO_SUSPEND : 0),
 						dev_name(tps->dev), tps);
 	} else {
 		dev_warn(tps->dev, "Unable to find the interrupt, switching to polling\n");
@@ -2771,10 +2824,10 @@ int tipd_init(struct tps6598x *tps)
 
 	fwnode_handle_put(fwnode);
 
-	tps->wakeup = device_property_read_bool(tps->dev, "wakeup-source");
 	if (tps->wakeup && tps->irq) {
 		devm_device_init_wakeup(tps->dev);
-		enable_irq_wake(tps->irq);
+		if (!tps->sleep_event)
+			enable_irq_wake(tps->irq);
 	}
 
 	tipd_debugfs_register(tps);
@@ -2843,8 +2896,10 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(tipd_remove);
 int tipd_suspend(struct tps6598x *tps)
 {
 	if (tps->wakeup) {
-		disable_irq(tps->irq);
-		enable_irq_wake(tps->irq);
+		if (!tps->sleep_event) {
+			disable_irq(tps->irq);
+			enable_irq_wake(tps->irq);
+		}
 	} else if (tps->reset) {
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(tps->reset, 1);
 	}
@@ -2874,8 +2929,10 @@ int tipd_resume(struct tps6598x *tps)
 	}
 
 	if (tps->wakeup) {
-		disable_irq_wake(tps->irq);
-		enable_irq(tps->irq);
+		if (!tps->sleep_event) {
+			disable_irq_wake(tps->irq);
+			enable_irq(tps->irq);
+		}
 	} else if (tps->reset) {
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(tps->reset, 0);
 		msleep(TPS_SETUP_MS);
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/sn201202x-pm-test.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/sn201202x-pm-test.c
index 1082774dba..1d0efec7fa 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/sn201202x-pm-test.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/sn201202x-pm-test.c
@@ -220,12 +220,55 @@ static void sn201202x_unconfirmed_sleep_failed_wakeup_test(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, sn201202x_test_irq_enabled(t));
 }
 
+/* As read on a J713, the dock aside */
+static const struct cd321x_sleep_state sn201202x_test_charger_attach = {
+	/* Attached as a USB3 device, before the data role swap */
+	.data_status = 0x800000e1, .status = 0x1000600d,
+};
+
+static const struct cd321x_sleep_state sn201202x_test_charger_swapped = {
+	/* A USB3 link as host for a moment after it, then none */
+	.data_status = 0x80000061, .status = 0x1000904d,
+};
+
+static const struct cd321x_sleep_state sn201202x_test_charger = {
+	.data_status = 0x80000001, .status = 0x100c90cd,
+};
+
+static const struct cd321x_sleep_state sn201202x_test_keyboard = {
+	/* Powered by this port, as are hubs */
+	.data_status = 0x00000073, .status = 0x100000fd,
+};
+
+static const struct cd321x_sleep_state sn201202x_test_dock = {
+	/* Powers this port and passes USB: a USB capable source */
+	.data_status = 0x80000073, .status = 0x100c90cd, .usb_comm = true,
+};
+
+/* In system sleep a charger is no link; a USB device, dock or display is. */
+static void sn201202x_sleep_links_test(struct kunit *test)
+{
+	struct cd321x_sleep_state dp = {
+		.data_status = TPS_DATA_STATUS_DATA_CONNECTION |
+			       TPS_DATA_STATUS_DP_CONNECTION,
+		.status = 0x100c90cd,
+	};
+
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sn201202x_sleep_links(&sn201202x_test_charger_attach), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sn201202x_sleep_links(&sn201202x_test_charger_swapped), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sn201202x_sleep_links(&sn201202x_test_charger), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_NE(test, sn201202x_sleep_links(&sn201202x_test_keyboard), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_NE(test, sn201202x_sleep_links(&sn201202x_test_dock), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sn201202x_sleep_links(&dp), TPS_DATA_STATUS_DP_CONNECTION);
+}
+
 static struct kunit_case sn201202x_pm_cases[] = {
 	KUNIT_CASE(sn201202x_sleep_cycle_test),
 	KUNIT_CASE(sn201202x_failed_wakeup_test),
 	KUNIT_CASE(sn201202x_rejected_sleep_test),
 	KUNIT_CASE(sn201202x_unconfirmed_sleep_test),
 	KUNIT_CASE(sn201202x_unconfirmed_sleep_failed_wakeup_test),
+	KUNIT_CASE(sn201202x_sleep_links_test),
 	{}
 };
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
index 144a4787c5..039ce7b214 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 
 #include <kunit/visibility.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
@@ -8,12 +9,16 @@
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/spmi.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/usb/role.h>
 
 #include "tps6598x.h"
 
 #define tps_to_sn(tps) container_of_const((tps), struct sn201202x, cd.tps)
 
+/* A sleeping controller does not answer a select; give up on it sooner. */
+#define SN201202X_ATOMIC_SELECT_MS	10
+
 static int regmap_sn201202x_select_reg(struct spmi_device *sdev, u8 reg)
 {
 	int err;
@@ -35,9 +40,15 @@ static int regmap_sn201202x_select_reg(struct spmi_device *sdev, u8 reg)
 	if (sn->polled || sn->select_polled) {
 		int poll_err;
 
-		poll_err = read_poll_timeout(spmi_register_read, err,
-					     err || val == reg, 100, 100000,
-					     false, sdev, 0, &val);
+		if (sn->atomic)
+			poll_err = read_poll_timeout_atomic(spmi_register_read, err,
+							    err || val == reg, 100,
+							    SN201202X_ATOMIC_SELECT_MS * 1000,
+							    false, sdev, 0, &val);
+		else
+			poll_err = read_poll_timeout(spmi_register_read, err,
+						     err || val == reg, 100, 100000,
+						     false, sdev, 0, &val);
 		return err ?: poll_err;
 	}
 
@@ -174,8 +185,15 @@ static const struct of_device_id sn201202x_of_match[] = {
 	{}
 };
 
-static int sn201202x_wake(struct sn201202x *sn)
+/*
+ * In system sleep the wake interrupt is suspended, so the controller is
+ * polled as without interrupts.
+ */
+static int sn201202x_wake_poll(struct sn201202x *sn, bool poll)
 {
+	/* Busy-waiting has no clock to go by: each step is charged instead */
+	int budget_ms = 500;
+	unsigned int tries = 0;
 	unsigned long deadline;
 	u8 size;
 	int ret;
@@ -184,16 +202,24 @@ static int sn201202x_wake(struct sn201202x *sn)
 	ret = spmi_command_wakeup(sn->sdev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	if (!sn->polled)
-		return wait_for_completion_timeout(&sn->wake_completion,
-						   msecs_to_jiffies(100)) ? 0 : -ETIMEDOUT;
+	/* A WAKEUP sent while it was still going to sleep may go unanswered */
+	if (!poll && wait_for_completion_timeout(&sn->wake_completion,
+						 msecs_to_jiffies(100)))
+		return 0;
 
 	/* A sleeping ACE3 ACKs commands but returns zeros until it is awake. */
 	deadline = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(500);
 	do {
+		if (++tries % 20 == 0) {
+			ret = spmi_command_wakeup(sn->sdev);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+		}
 		ret = regmap_sn201202x_select_reg(sn->sdev, TPS_REG_MODE);
-		if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
+		if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT) {
+			budget_ms -= SN201202X_ATOMIC_SELECT_MS;
 			continue;
+		}
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 		ret = spmi_register_read(sn->sdev, 0x1f, &size);
@@ -201,12 +227,77 @@ static int sn201202x_wake(struct sn201202x *sn)
 			return ret;
 		if (size)
 			return 0;
-		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
-	} while (time_before(jiffies, deadline));
+		if (sn->atomic)
+			mdelay(1);
+		else
+			usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+		budget_ms--;
+	} while (sn->atomic ? budget_ms > 0 : time_before(jiffies, deadline));
 
 	return -ETIMEDOUT;
 }
 
+static int sn201202x_wake(struct sn201202x *sn)
+{
+	return sn201202x_wake_poll(sn, sn->polled);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The links that wake the system when they appear in system sleep. A port
+ * attaches as a USB device before any data role swap, as it does to a
+ * charger, and a charger may still show a USB link for a moment after one:
+ * a USB link counts only with this port as the host, and from a power source
+ * only if the source is capable of USB communication.
+ */
+VISIBLE_IF_KUNIT u32 sn201202x_sleep_links(const struct cd321x_sleep_state *st)
+{
+	u32 links = st->data_status & (TPS_DATA_STATUS_DP_CONNECTION |
+				       TPS_DATA_STATUS_TBT_CONNECTION |
+				       CD321X_DATA_STATUS_USB4_CONNECTION);
+
+	if (st->data_status & TPS_DATA_STATUS_USB_DATA_ROLE)
+		return links;
+	if (!(st->status & TPS_STATUS_PORTROLE) && !st->usb_comm)
+		return links;
+	return links | (st->data_status & (TPS_DATA_STATUS_USB2_CONNECTION |
+					   TPS_DATA_STATUS_USB3_CONNECTION));
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_IF_KUNIT(sn201202x_sleep_links);
+
+/*
+ * The event interrupt stays live in system sleep (IRQF_NO_SUSPEND). Wake the
+ * controller to acknowledge the event, and wake the system only for a new
+ * data connection, or if the controller cannot be read. It goes back to sleep
+ * either way, as the resume expects.
+ */
+static bool sn201202x_sleep_event(struct tps6598x *tps)
+{
+	struct sn201202x *sn = tps_to_sn(tps);
+	struct cd321x_sleep_state st;
+	u32 links = 0;
+	bool wake;
+	int ret;
+
+	guard(mutex)(&tps->lock);
+	if (!READ_ONCE(sn->sleep_watch))
+		return false;
+
+	sn->atomic = true;
+	ret = sn201202x_wake_poll(sn, true);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = cd321x_sleep_events(tps, &st);
+	if (!ret)
+		links = sn201202x_sleep_links(&st);
+	wake = ret || (links & ~sn->sleep_links);
+	if (!ret)
+		sn->sleep_links = links;
+	spmi_command_sleep(sn->sdev);
+	sn->atomic = false;
+	if (wake)
+		pm_wakeup_dev_event(tps->dev, 0, true);
+	return true;
+}
+
 static int sn201202x_probe(struct spmi_device *device)
 {
 	const struct of_device_id *match;
@@ -292,6 +383,13 @@ static int sn201202x_probe(struct spmi_device *device)
 			return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * In system sleep only the event interrupt stays live. Register access
+	 * then has to poll, which a select notification would not.
+	 */
+	if (!sn->polled && sn->select_polled)
+		tps->sleep_event = sn201202x_sleep_event;
+
 	spmi_device_set_drvdata(device, tps);
 	tps->regmap = devm_regmap_init_sn201202x(device, &tps6598x_regmap_config);
 	if (IS_ERR(tps->regmap))
@@ -322,6 +420,11 @@ VISIBLE_IF_KUNIT int __maybe_unused sn201202x_resume(struct device *dev)
 	struct sn201202x *sn = tps_to_sn(tps);
 	int err;
 
+	if (READ_ONCE(sn->sleep_watch)) {
+		/* Waits for a running sleep_event() */
+		disable_irq(tps->irq);
+		WRITE_ONCE(sn->sleep_watch, false);
+	}
 	err = sn201202x_wake(sn);
 	if (!err)
 		err = tipd_resume(tps);
@@ -336,6 +439,7 @@ VISIBLE_IF_KUNIT int __maybe_unused sn201202x_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct tps6598x *tps = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct sn201202x *sn = tps_to_sn(tps);
+	bool watch;
 	int err, ret;
 
 	/*
@@ -348,6 +452,19 @@ VISIBLE_IF_KUNIT int __maybe_unused sn201202x_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	err = tipd_suspend(tps);
 	if (err)
 		goto out_enable;
+	watch = tps->sleep_event && device_may_wakeup(dev) &&
+		pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE;
+	if (watch) {
+		struct cd321x_sleep_state st;
+
+		guard(mutex)(&tps->lock);
+		/* Without a baseline, a plug-in in sleep cannot be told from a charger */
+		watch = !cd321x_sleep_events(tps, &st);
+		if (watch)
+			sn->sleep_links = sn201202x_sleep_links(&st);
+		else
+			dev_warn(dev, "port state unreadable, no wakeup for an attach\n");
+	}
 	reinit_completion(&sn->sleep_completion);
 	err = spmi_command_sleep(sn->sdev);
 	if (err)
@@ -357,6 +474,10 @@ VISIBLE_IF_KUNIT int __maybe_unused sn201202x_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 		goto out_wake;
 	}
+	if (watch) {
+		WRITE_ONCE(sn->sleep_watch, true);
+		enable_irq(tps->irq);
+	}
 	return 0;
 
 out_wake:
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h
index 305ac3a269..f9455bdc76 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h
@@ -357,6 +357,8 @@ struct tps6598x {
 	enum power_supply_usb_type usb_type;
 
 	int wakeup;
+	/* Handles events while the system sleeps, if the variant can filter them */
+	bool (*sleep_event)(struct tps6598x *tps);
 	u32 status; /* status reg */
 	u32 data_status;
 	u16 pwr_status;
@@ -452,6 +454,11 @@ struct sn201202x {
 	struct completion sleep_completion;
 	struct completion wake_completion;
 	struct spmi_device *sdev;
+	/* Links that wake the system, while the controller's events are filtered */
+	u32 sleep_links;
+	bool sleep_watch;
+	/* Busy-wait: in suspend-to-idle a sleeping wait outlasts the timers */
+	bool atomic;
 };
 
 extern const struct tipd_data *tipd_hw_variants[];
@@ -466,6 +473,15 @@ int tipd_resume(struct tps6598x *tps);
 
 /* Internal to tps6598x-core */
 int tps6598x_block_read(struct tps6598x *tps, u8 reg, void *val, size_t len);
+/* What the system-sleep event filter of a port reads */
+struct cd321x_sleep_state {
